&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VLA Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Integrate VLA models into the robots&#39; software stack to drive manipulation and task execution on humanoid and industrial platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Software Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement software components and architectures for AI-enhanced robotics applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Develop applications that keep working across a changing set of robots and sensors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stack Maintenance:&lt;/strong&gt; Review and maintain the shared software stack used across humanoid and close-to-industry robot projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Research Integration:&lt;/strong&gt; Track new developments in robotics and AI software, and bring promising external components into the stack alongside in-house development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Background:&lt;/strong&gt; Degree in robotics, computer science, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, or a related field, or equivalent qualification, together with around four years building software for robotic systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;VLA Models:&lt;/strong&gt; Hands-on experience building or integrating vision-language-action models on physical robots.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Stack:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency in C++, CMake, Python, shell scripting, and Git for building and maintaining production robotics software.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ROS 2:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience building robot software on ROS 2.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Beneficial Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Robot Platforms:&lt;/strong&gt; Experience working with dual-arm or humanoid robot platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Computer Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Working knowledge of computer vision and robot control methods.&lt;/li&gt;
